      "topic": "Test Listeners & Automated Screenshot Capture on Failure",
      "question": "How do you automatically attach screenshots, DOM snapshots, and error stack traces to your test report only when a test fails?",
      "expectedFocus": "TestNG ITestListener (onTestFailure) in Selenium or Playwright config screenshot: \"only-on-failure\", trace: \"retain-on-failure\".",
      "answerSummary": "### 1. Conceptual Breakdown (Plain English)\n**What it is:** In Selenium TestNG, implement ITestListener and override onTestFailure(ITestResult result).\n**Why it matters in QA:** Understanding this concept enables QA engineers to bridge the gap between business specifications and technical verification, eliminating guesswork and test flakiness.\n\n### 2. Deep-Dive Technical Explanation\nIn Selenium TestNG, implement ITestListener and override onTestFailure(ITestResult result). Cast driver to TakesScreenshot, capture the file as base64 or png, and attach it to ExtentReports or Allure. In Playwright, configure use: { screenshot: \"only-on-failure\", trace: \"retain-on-failure\", video: \"retain-on-failure\" } in playwright.config.ts.\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Practical Application Guide\n• **Step 1: Identify Preconditions & Scope:** Clarify the exact system boundary, inputs, and expected environmental states before executing.\n• **Step 2: Construct Deterministic Assertions:** Avoid relying on arbitrary delays; instead, assert against explicit system state transitions and verifiable outcomes.\n• **Step 3: Isolate Environmental Variables:** Ensure test data is cleanly provisioned and cleaned up so parallel or subsequent runs remain independent.\n\n### 4. Key Terminology for QA Engineers\n• **Deterministic Testing:** A testing approach where a given input always produces the exact same observable outcome without intermittent or random failures.\n• **Flakiness (Flaky Test):** A test that intermittently passes and fails on identical application builds without any code changes, usually caused by timing race conditions or shared mutable state.\n• **Quality Gate:** An automated checkpoint in the CI/CD pipeline that blocks flawed builds from progressing to staging or production.",
      "codeSnippet": "// TestNG Listener onTestFailure:\n@Override\npublic void onTestFailure(ITestResult result) {\n  WebDriver driver = DriverManager.getDriver();\n  byte[] screenshot = ((TakesScreenshot) driver).getScreenshotAs(OutputType.BYTES);\n  Allure.addAttachment(\"Failure Screenshot\", new ByteArrayInputStream(screenshot));\n}",
      "bestPractice": "Attach request/response HTTP headers and browser console logs alongside failure screenshots for rapid debugging.",
      "pitfallToAvoid": "Capturing video and screenshots for 100% of passing tests in CI, consuming gigabytes of disk and slowing execution.",
      "technology": "Quality Engineering"
